      "value": "That means extra tab in menu, and most users don't need it because they can block avatars in Security tab to allow ONLY friends and trusted users. Visitors / New can blocked so less (useless) downloads for you.\n\nSo there are already small solutions for it. You can select user to block.\nI don't think we all need the new tab to see download queue because it will mostly fast and it's already done.\n\nWorld size in MB is visible in World info, check it first before you go to the world. If you hate download many avatars, don't enter busy world, take one with 10 users or less to start better. Or prepare more downloading if you enter world with 30 users.\n\nAnd youtube videos... it's stream btw. Like you watch in your browser. Ask owner don't use that youtube stream or so, or don't enter world with cinema screen. There are plenty worlds without cinema screen.\n\nSo here are steps:\n- check world info page first for world size (you cannot split it anyway, it must download whole package)\n- set your security settings to ignore visitors / new users avatar. You can even block everything. Once you made friends the avatar will downloaded. Or don't enter very busy world.\n- ask owner don't start youtube stream if world has TV / cinema screen.\n- Set your home world in light weight world, not one of the heavy worlds. (that is where you will start - to reduce waiting to load first world)\n\nThere are solutions, so think forward and check security settings, then you're fine for most time. And most users are happy with VRChat so the download queue is not really needed.\nAvatars are downloaded once you're in the world room. That's why you should not enter very busy world.\n\nDon't go to the avatar worlds where are like 100 avatars seen in ONE room. That is a lot downloading avatars information. They're bad build avatar worlds. Good avatar worlds have more rooms to reduce downloading once for each room, because it will only show once you enter the room. (i know there are poor/heavy avatar worlds with too much avatars in one room)\n\nAnd make sure cache room is big enough, at least 10GB. Otherwise you must block almost all avatars. Or buy better PC, it's no fun to play VRChat if your disk room is almost full. That won't do.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
