      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bcbaf75fab2337b72ced6b0|full_name}: There are a few problems with this, blocking an avatar currently does not stop the download, even if someone enters a world for a split second, once the avatar download process starts, it continues until it is done, this can queue up already and not allow you to download any avatars in the world. The file size of worlds and amount of people in the world is impossible to know on private maps when your just browsing through your friends list. Downloading avatars/worlds isn't always fast and its impossible currently to tell who's avatar is what file size and as soon as the process starts, it won't stop unless restarted. Videos are fine most of the time, but after entering a world with a stream, I find it still downloading the stream in the background until the stream has ended.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
